# The sum of two intervals with 2-limb bounds. A bound that the finite cores do not return as a
# finite number (an unbounded operand, or an overflow) becomes the infinity on its side; an
# empty operand gives the empty set. Not in gen/kernels yet: Clang 18 at -O2 computes the scalar
# code's independent FMAs two to a packed instruction (SLP vectorization), and the generator's
# object-code check, one fused instruction per FMA, cannot count those.
kernel:        interval_add_2
input:         xl = xl0 xl1
input:         xu = xu0 xu1
input:         yl = yl0 yl1
input:         yu = yu0 yu1
output:        zl = zl0 zl1
output:        zu = zu0 zu1
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
ieee_only:     yes
cone_exempt:   every output is selected after explicit tests of the bounds (fl, fh) and of the operands (ne)

(l0, l1) = add_down_2_2(xl0, xl1, yl0, yl1)
(h0, h1) = add_up_2_2(xu0, xu1, yu0, yu1)
al  = abs(l0)
fl  = lt(al, const inf)
ah  = abs(h0)
fh  = lt(ah, const inf)
mi  = neg(const inf)
a0  = select(fl, l0, mi)
a1  = select(fl, l1, 0)
b0  = select(fh, h0, const inf)
b1  = select(fh, h1, 0)
nx  = lt(xl0, const inf)
ny  = lt(yl0, const inf)
ne  = and(nx, ny)
zl0 = select(ne, a0, const inf)
zl1 = select(ne, a1, 0)
zu0 = select(ne, b0, mi)
zu1 = select(ne, b1, 0)
